{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And it kills a man or a woman.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded that this verse is set free for the purpose of drawing a gezerah shavah to judge from it all cases of damages in the Torah — the same for a man and the same for a woman. And even though we do not now adjudicate the laws of fines, nevertheless if he seized we do not remove it from him. And we excommunicate that man who established a hazard in his house. From Rabbi Natan: from where do we know that a person should not raise a vicious dog within his house? As it is said (Deuteronomy 22): ״ולא תשים דמים בביתך״. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said in Bava Kamma: this one who wishes to be a pietist must be scrupulous in matters of damages. The early pietists would bury their thorns and their glass in their fields and deepen them three handbreadths so that the plow would not bring them up. And there was an incident involving a certain man who was clearing stones from a house and threw them into the public domain. An elder said to him: 'Empty one, why are you clearing from a place that is not yours to a place that is yours?' That man mocked him. Days later, the man was in need and sold his house and stumbled over those very stones. He immediately recalled the words of that elder and said: 'He spoke well to me — why are you clearing stones from a place that is not yours to a place that is yours?' And this is what the verse says (Ecclesiastes 12): ״וזכור את בוראיך בימי בחורותיך״." "<b>And its owner shall also be put to death.</b> This is not by human courts, for our Rabbis of blessed memory said: for the murder of the person you kill him, but you do not kill him for the murder of his ox; rather, it is by the hand of Heaven, in the language of (Numbers 3): ״והזר הקרב יומת״, (Leviticus 22): ״ומתו בו כי יחללוהו״ — the meaning of which is by the hand of Heaven."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "Citation reads (דברים כב); the verse quoted is Deuteronomy 22:8. Citation reads (קהלת יב); the verse quoted is Ecclesiastes 12:1.", 1 "Citation reads (במדבר ג); the verse quoted is Numbers 3:10. Citation reads (ויקרא כב); the verse quoted is Leviticus 22:9."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:48.412591080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}